"""
hilde-launcher, the programme behind hilde run: it starts the ranks of a Sperli job on the hosts of a list.

- The compiler hands it the words after run.
- It reads the host list, makes the keys and certificates of the job and starts one process for each rank.
- A rank on this machine is started directly, any other over ssh at port 62222; a host that Standard.SperliWire refuses is refused even if listed.
- The exit status is 0 when every rank ended with 0, 2 for a command line it does not take, else the largest status of a rank.

    hilde run -n 3 --hosts hosts.txt ./app
"""
module Run.Main is
    """
    The programme: reads the command line and runs the job.
    No contract: the exit code is the work of the programme.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
